cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use Terik in your work, please cite it as below.
type: software
title: 'Terik: heat stress forecasts and a 65-year heat record'
abstract: >-
  A web app that turns weather forecasts and ERA5 reanalysis into wet bulb
  globe temperature (WBGT) with the Liljegren et al. (2008) model, and into
  work, sport and football advice based on NIOSH, ACSM and FIFPRO guidance.
  All calculations run in the browser.
authors:
  - given-names: Raffa Gamadan
    family-names: Rifandi
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-09-30
license: MIT
repository-code: https://github.com/ResVet/terik
url: https://terik.netlify.app
keywords:
  - heat stress
  - wet bulb globe temperature
  - WBGT
  - occupational heat exposure
  - ERA5
  - climate trends
references:
  - type: article
    title: Modeling the wet bulb globe temperature using standard meteorological measurements
    authors:
      - family-names: Liljegren
        given-names: J. C.
      - family-names: Carhart
        given-names: R. A.
      - family-names: Lawday
        given-names: P.
      - family-names: Tschopp
        given-names: S.
      - family-names: Sharp
        given-names: R.
    journal: Journal of Occupational and Environmental Hygiene
    volume: 5
    issue: '10'
    start: 645
    end: 655
    year: 2008
    doi: 10.1080/15459620802310770
